    "PROGRAM_BOOT_PRINT_ERROR": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Boots the DOS session from a floppy or hard disk image, in Bochs IMG format.\n\nUsage: \u001b[34;1mboot [\"Image 1.img\" \"Image 2.img\" ...] -L [A/C/D]\u001b[0m\n\nAccepts one or more floppy disk images (swap them by pressing Cmd-R)\nor a single hard disk image. \n\n\u001b[32;1m-L\u001b[0m specifies which drive letter to boot from: \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m, \u001b[32;1mC\u001b[0m or \u001b[32;1mD\u001b[0m (default is \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m.)\nTo boot from a hard disk image, it must first be mounted with the\n\u001b[34;1mimgmount\u001b[0m command.\n\n"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Inicia la sesiÃ³n DOS desde un disquete o una imagen de disco duro, en formato \nBochs IMG.\n\nUso:   \u001b[34;1mboot [\"Imagen 1.img\" \"Imagen 2.img\" ...] -L [A/C/D]\u001b[0m\n\nAcepta una o mÃ¡s imÃ¡genes de disquete (intercambiarlas al presionar Cmd-R)\no una imagen individual de disco duro.\n\n\u001b[32;1m-L\u001b[0m especifica la letra de unidad para iniciar desde: \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m, \u001b[32;1mC\u001b[0m o \u001b[32;1mD\u001b[0m\n(por defecto es \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m.)\nPara iniciar desde una imagen de disco duro, primero se debe montar\ncon el comando \u001b[34;1mimgmount\u001b[0m.\n\n"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "DÃ©marre la session DOS Ã  partir d'une image de disquette ou de disque dur,\nau format IMG Bochs.\n\nUsage : \u001b[34;1mboot [\"Image 1.img\" \"Image 2.img\" ...] -L [A/C/D]\u001b[0m\n\nAccepte une ou plusieurs images de disquette (permutez en appuyant sur Cmd-R)\nou une image de disque dur simple.\n\n\u001b[32;1m-L\u001b[0m spÃ©cifie la lettre de lecteur Ã  utiliser pour dÃ©marrer : \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m, \u001b[32;1mC\u001b[0m ou \u001b[32;1mD\u001b[0m\n(par dÃ©faut : \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m).\nPour dÃ©marrer Ã  partir d'une image de disque dur, elle doit d'abord Ãªtre montÃ©e\navec la commande \u001b[34;1mimgmount\u001b[0m.\n\n"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Boots the DOS session from a floppy or hard disk image, in Bochs IMG format.\n\nUsage: \u001b[34;1mboot [\"Image 1.img\" \"Image 2.img\" ...] -L [A/C/D]\u001b[0m\n\nAccepts one or more floppy disk images (swap them by pressing Cmd-R)\nor a single hard disk image. \n\n\u001b[32;1m-L\u001b[0m specifies which drive letter to boot from: \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m, \u001b[32;1mC\u001b[0m or \u001b[32;1mD\u001b[0m (default is \u001b[32;1mA\u001b[0m.)\nTo boot from a hard disk image, it must first be mounted with the\n\u001b[34;1mimgmount\u001b[0m command.\n\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
