    "PROGRAM_IMGMOUNT_SPECIFY_DRIVE": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Makes the contents of an ISO/CUE/IMG disk image into a DOS drive.\n\nUsage:   \u001b[34;1mimgmount [DOS drive letter] [\"Path/to/image.iso\"] -t [hdd/floppy/iso]\u001b[0m\nExample: \u001b[32;1mimgmount d \"/Users/yourname/Desktop/Game.iso\" -t iso\u001b[0m will mount\nthe Game.iso disk image as the D: drive.\n\nYou can specify what kind of drive to use by adding the \u001b[34;1m-t\u001b[0m parameter:\n\u001b[32;1m-t hdd\u001b[0m mounts it as a hard disk.\n\u001b[32;1m-t iso\u001b[0m mounts it as a CD-ROM.\n\u001b[32;1m-t floppy\u001b[0m mounts it as a floppy disk.\n"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Prepara el contenido de una imagen de disco ISO/CUE/IMG en una unidad DOS.\n\nUso:   \u001b[34;1mimgmount [letra de unidad DOS] [\"Ruta/a/image.iso\"] -t [hdd/floppy/iso]\u001b[0m\nEjemplo: \u001b[32;1mimgmount d \"/Users/yourname/Desktop/Game.iso\" -t iso\u001b[0m montarÃ¡\nla imagen de disco Game.iso como la unidad D:.\n\nPuede especificar que tipo de unidad usar al aÃ±adir el parÃ¡metro \u001b[34;1m-t\u001b[0m:\n\u001b[32;1m-t hdd\u001b[0m monta como disco duro.\n\u001b[32;1m-t iso\u001b[0m monta como CD-ROM.\n\u001b[32;1m-t floppy\u001b[0m monta como disquete.\n"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Place le contenu d'une image disque ISO/CUE/IMG dans un lecteur DOS.\n\nUsage :   \u001b[34;1mimgmount [lettre DOS] [\"Chemin/de/image.iso\"] -t [hdd/floppy/iso]\u001b[0m\nExemple : \u001b[32;1mimgmount d \"/Users/votrenom/Desktop/Jeu.iso\" -t iso\u001b[0m montera\n\t\t  l'image disque Jeu.iso en tant que lecteur D:.\n\nVous pouvez spÃ©cifier le type de lecteur Ã  utiliser avec le paramÃ¨tre \u001b[34;1m-t\u001b[0m :\n\u001b[32;1m-t hdd\u001b[0m monte en tant que disque dur.\n\u001b[32;1m-t iso\u001b[0m monte en tant que CD-ROM.\n\u001b[32;1m-t floppy\u001b[0m monte en tant que disquette.\n"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Makes the contents of an ISO/CUE/IMG disk image into a DOS drive.\n\nUsage:   \u001b[34;1mimgmount [DOS drive letter] [\"Path/to/image.iso\"] -t [hdd/floppy/iso]\u001b[0m\nExample: \u001b[32;1mimgmount d \"/Users/yourname/Desktop/Game.iso\" -t iso\u001b[0m will mount\nthe Game.iso disk image as the D: drive.\n\nYou can specify what kind of drive to use by adding the \u001b[34;1m-t\u001b[0m parameter:\n\u001b[32;1m-t hdd\u001b[0m mounts it as a hard disk.\n\u001b[32;1m-t iso\u001b[0m mounts it as a CD-ROM.\n\u001b[32;1m-t floppy\u001b[0m mounts it as a floppy disk.\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "PROGRAM_IMGMOUNT_SPECIFY2": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Please specify which drive number to mount the image at:\n0 = Floppy drive 1\n1 = Floppy drive 2\n2 = Hard drive 1\n3 = Hard drive 2\n"
          }
        },
        "es": {
